//- IP allow / deny lists; swapped as a whole after every change. Needs page, rules (IpRuleDto[]), me.
- import neko.platform.presentation.web.icons : icon;
- import neko.platform.presentation.web.support : shortTime;
.card#ip-rules
  - if (rules.length == 0)
    .card-body
      p.text-secondary.mb-0 No IP rules: every address may reach every area (the firewall still applies). Add allow rules to limit the management pages or the APIs to known networks.
  - else
    .table-responsive
      table.table.table-vcenter.card-table
        thead
          tr
            th List
            th Network
            th Applies to
            th Note
            th.text-nowrap Added (UTC)
            - if (page.isSecurityManage)
              th.w-1
        tbody
          - foreach (r; rules)
            tr
              td
                - if (r.action == "allow")
                  span.badge.bg-green-lt
                    | !{icon("circle-check")}
                    | allow
                - else
                  span.badge.bg-red-lt
                    | !{icon("ban")}
                    | deny
              td
                code= r.network
              td= r.scope_ == "all" ? "everything (also the public site)" : r.scope_ == "admin" ? "management pages" : "APIs (REST, OData, /api, /metrics)"
              td.text-secondary= r.note
              td.text-nowrap.text-secondary
                div= shortTime(r.createdAt)
                .small= r.createdBy
              - if (page.isSecurityManage)
                td
                  button.btn.btn-ghost-danger.btn-icon(hx-post="/security/rules/#{r.id}/delete", hx-target="#ip-rules", hx-swap="outerHTML", hx-confirm="Remove #{r.network} from the #{r.action} list?", title="Remove", aria-label="Remove #{r.network}")
                    | !{icon("trash")}
  .card-footer.small.text-secondary
    | A deny rule blocks matching addresses. Where allow rules exist for an area, only the listed networks reach it. Changes that would lock you out (#{me.length ? me : "local"}) are refused; the CLI (firewall …) always works.
